 822	    ///
 823	    /// Bounded and safe:
 824	    /// - the primary attempt runs first;
 825	    /// - failover is attempted only when [`failover_eligible`] is true — i.e. the
 826	    ///   attempt streamed *no* output (so no model output / tool side effect can
 827	    ///   be replayed) **and** the error is transient/availability. A mid-stream
 828	    ///   failure, a user/content error, or a cancellation is returned as-is;
 829	    /// - at most ONE alternate is tried (the highest-priority ready provider
 830	    ///   other than the one that just failed), so failover can never fan out or
 831	    ///   loop. If the alternate also fails, its error is returned.
